    "created_at": "2020-08-29T17:25:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-29T17:25:32Z",
    "body": "I think the `missing-credentials` error is incorrect. That error occurs if there is an `@` but no host. `https://@test.com` should not cause the parser to fail, but `https://username:password@` should (and does, in the Live URL viewer in Safari 13).\r\n\r\nPerhaps it should be replaced by something like 'unexpected credentials without host' (similar to 'unexpected port without host')?",
